# Recipe Backend API

A RESTful API for managing recipes, built with **Node.js**, **Express.js**, and **MongoDB** using **Mongoose**.  
The application follows the **MVC pattern** and provides full **CRUD operations** for recipes.

# Postman documentation link
https://.postman.co/workspace/My-Workspace~2149278c-1536-4e00-85db-649400f80d1f/collection/40357180-d7e06ec6-4612-4d13-a8c4-fb76941a2fd9?action=share&creator=40357180

---

## ✅ Features

- Create a new recipe
- Read all recipes
- Read a single recipe by ID
- Update a recipe by ID
- Delete a recipe by ID
- Input validation using `express-validator`
- Error handling for invalid requests
- Follows MVC architecture
- Fully deployable on **Render**

---

## 🛠 Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js
- **Database:** MongoDB (Mongoose ODM)
- **Validation:** express-validator
- **API Testing:** Postman
- **Deployment:** Render

---

## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

1. Clone the repository:


git clone <your-github-repo-url>
cd Recipe-Backend
Install dependencies:

bash
Copy code
npm install
Create a .env file in the root directory:

ini
Copy code
MONGO_URI=<your-mongodb-atlas-connection-string>
Run the server locally:

bash
Copy code
npm start
Server runs on:

arduino
Copy code
http://localhost:3000
🌐 API Endpoints
Base URL: https://your-deployed-app.onrender.com/api/recipes

Method	Endpoint	Description	Body (JSON) Example
GET	/api/recipes	Get all recipes	—
GET	/api/recipes/:id	Get recipe by ID	—
POST	/api/recipes	Create a new recipe	{ "title": "Pasta", "ingredients": ["noodles", "sauce"], "instructions": "Boil noodles and mix sauce." }
PUT	/api/recipes/:id	Update recipe by ID	{ "title": "Updated Pasta" }
DELETE	/api/recipes/:id	Delete recipe by ID	—

⚠️ Error Handling
Invalid IDs or missing recipes return 404 Not Found.

Server errors return 500 Internal Server Error with the error message.

📌 Notes
Always use the _id returned after creating a recipe for GET, PUT, DELETE requests.

Make sure the .env variables are correctly set for MongoDB connection.

Deployments on Render require process.env.PORT to be used.

